Condition : 21 - No unit shall be occupied until a Car Park Management Plan has been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The Plan shall include the following:
o	Details and location of 20% electric vehicle charging points (min. 7kW/h) and details of a further 20% passive provision;
o	A strategy detailing how the uptake in electric vehicle charging points is monitored to bring into use passive charging points when required;
o	Details of parking layout and allocations
o	Details of how parking outside of designated bays will be managed;
Details to prevent the sale of parking spaces with flats and leasing arrangements to facilitate parking for those who require a space to park.
The car parking areas shall thereafter be managed in compliance with the approved Car Park Management Plan.
Reason: In order to promote sustainable modes of transport and safeguard the amenities of surrounding residential properties and ensure minimal disruption of traffic in the locality, in accordance with policies CC1, CC2 and EC2 of the adopted Local Plan and Policy 6.13 of the London Plan 2015.
